    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-052: GTK Viewport Height Threading**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (2 commits, ~40 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Closes ADR-051's Deferred item**: \"GTK allocated height threading to `render_pipeline`.\"\n\n## Measurement (2026-11-01)\n\n| Finding | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `render_pipeline.cpp` passes `viewport_height` | **0.0f** (line 328) |\n| `on_draw` tracks `m_last_width` | Yes |\n| `on_draw` tracks `m_last_height` | **No** |\n| `render_html` / `render_with_css` query widget height | **None** |\n| `relayout()` signature | `void relayout(float viewport_width)` only |\n\n### The critical widget distinction\n\n```\nHoneyBeeWindow\n  └─ m_scroll_window (Gtk::ScrolledWindow)     ← visible viewport (~800px)\n      └─ m_drawing_area (Gtk::DrawingArea)     ← content canvas (~60,000px on Wikipedia)\n```\n\n**`m_drawing_area.get_height()` returns content height** (~60,000px on Wikipedia). Feeding that to `LengthContext.viewport_h` would make `100vh = 60000` — catastrophically wrong.\n\n**`m_scroll_window.get_height()` returns visible viewport height** — exactly what CSS `vh` means.\n\n## GTK4 API note\n\nThe codebase is GTK4 (`m_drawing_area.get_width()` — no `get_allocated_width()`). In GTK4, `Widget::get_height()` **is** the allocated height (`get_allocated_height()` was removed in GTK3→GTK4 transition). So the correct call is `m_scroll_window.get_height()`.\n\n## Scope (2 commits)\n\n### Commit 1 — Threading + `m_last_height` (~40 lines)\n\n- 3 pipeline signature extensions with `viewport_height = 0.0f` (default protects ~15 test callers, same pattern as ADR-051)\n- `render_pipeline.cpp` forwards `viewport_height` to `layout_with_pseudo(...)`\n- `window.cpp`: `render_html` / `render_with_css` pass `m_scroll_window.get_height()`\n- `window.cpp`: `on_draw` tracks `m_last_height`, relayouts on **either** dimension change\n- `window.hpp`: `int m_last_height = 0;`\n\n### Commit 2 — Docs\n\n- ADR-052 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-052 note in ADR-051 (deferred item closed)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero visible delta.** Even with correct height threaded:\n\n1. `vh` feeds only `max-height` / `max-width`\n2. Layout doesn't read either (deferred to min/max clamp ADR)\n3. `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` still `h=0` from ancestor culling\n\n**What changes**:\n- `parse_length(\"calc(100vh - 48px)\")` returns `window_height - 48` in production (752 at typical 800px window, was -48 because viewport_h was 0)\n- Lands in `ComputedStyle.max-height` — correct semantically\n- Layout ignores it (no min/max clamp yet)\n\n**PNG delta: zero.** Documented honestly.\n\n## The definitive verification\n\n```bash\nHONEYBEE_LOG=layout ./build/bin/honeybee\n```\n\n**Before**: `[honeybee][layout][info] layout: viewport=1774x0`\n**After**:  `[honeybee][layout][info] layout: viewport=1774x800`\n\nThat's the proof — `viewport_h` is nonzero in production for the first time.\n\n## What this delivers\n\n- **ADR-051's Deferred item closed**\n- **One fewer prerequisite** on the sticky sidebar chain — the next cycle (max-height honoring) finds `viewport_h` already correct\n- **Correct `vh` semantics in production** for the first time\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Same as ADR-047/048**: correct infrastructure shipped before its consumer. Layout-tree verified via `HONEYBEE_LOG=layout` (viewport=1774x800 vs 1774x0); PNG zero-delta honestly recorded.\n\n## Test count\n\nNo tests added. Threading is mechanical; behavior verified via log + manual. All 644 existing tests pass unchanged (default param).\n\nRefs #236\n",
